 - Partner with the Principal Engineer on infrastructure strategy, capacity planning, reliability, and cost optimization.

What We Are Looking For:

 - 7+ years of commercial backend development experience with Node.js;

 - 3+ years in a technical leadership role such as Backend Lead, Team Lead, or Engineering Lead;

 - Experience leading and developing backend engineers, including mentoring and performance management;

 - 3+ years of hands-on production experience with NestJS;

 - Strong system design skills and proven experience designing and evolving microservice and distributed architectures;

 - Experience building and scaling high-load production systems;

 - Deep expertise in PostgreSQL and Redis, including performance optimization, data modeling, and caching strategies;

 - Experience with ORMs such as Prisma and Drizzle;

 - Hands-on experience with AWS, including EKS, RDS, SQS, S3, CloudWatch, and OpenSearch;

 - Strong practical knowledge of Docker and containerized environments;

 - Strong understanding of reliability, observability, monitoring, incident management, and on-call practices;

 - Ability to balance architectural strategy with hands-on engineering and pragmatic delivery;

 - Upper-Intermediate English or higher.

Nice To Have:

 - Active AWS Solutions Architect or Developer certification;

 - Experience with Terraform or other Infrastructure as Code tools;

 - Experience optimizing infrastructure and architecture for cost, latency, and performance at scale;

 - Payment systems integration experience;

 - Backend experience across both mobile applications and web products;

 - Experience with GCP and Cloudflare;

 - Experience hiring and scaling engineering teams in fast-growing product companies.

AI Expertise We Value:

 - Commercial experience integrating AI APIs such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, or other model providers;

 - Experience designing multi-model orchestration systems, including routing, fallbacks, retries, rate limits, and cost/latency optimization;

 - Understanding of production challenges around AI workloads, including reliability, observability, and provider dependencies;

 - Experience with AI-assisted engineering and code review tools such as Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, or similar;

 - Understanding of RAG, embeddings, vector search, MCP, and AI agents;

 - Hands-on production experience is a strong plus.

Why it’s exciting to work with us:

 - Take technical ownership of the backend platform behind a rapidly scaling AI product;

 - Shape architecture and engineering standards across a strong backend organization;

 - Work on real production challenges around high-load systems, AI orchestration, distributed architecture, and infrastructure at scale;

 - Build with cutting-edge AI technologies and directly influence how they are integrated into the product;

 - Join a strong engineering team with significant autonomy and direct impact on product and technical decisions;

 - Remote-first approach: work from anywhere, with the option to visit our offices in Warsaw and Kyiv;

 - Regular performance reviews with transparent growth and compensation discussions.

